# =====================================================================
# tgo-sandesh · Extreme or Nothing Protocol
# Copy to .env.local and fill. Every var below is READ somewhere in the
# code, and every process.env in the code has a var here. Nothing
# aspirational.
#
# NOT HERE, ON PURPOSE: the PRICE. It lives in src/app/_legal/legal.ts
# as PRICE.amount, which is this project's single source for it: the
# label the buyer reads, the paise Razorpay charges and the `value` on
# every Meta and GA4 event all resolve from that one number. Putting it
# in env would create a second source, and an unfilled env var would
# mean a page advertising 0 and a Razorpay order for zero paise with
# nothing throwing anywhere.
# =====================================================================


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# SITE
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# The live origin, with protocol and no trailing slash.
# e.g. https://extremeornothing.com
#
# Read by: src/app/layout.tsx (metadataBase, so a link pasted into
# WhatsApp does not preview as localhost) and src/lib/checkout-config.ts
# (fallbackEventSourceUrl, which is what Meta receives as
# event_source_url on the webhook's Purchase).
#
# WITHOUT IT: both fall back to the literal https://example.com, and
# every server-side Meta event is attributed to a domain nobody owns.
# The fallback literal appears in TWO files and they must match; both
# carry a matching PLACEHOLDER comment.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# BOOKING CALENDAR
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Sandesh's scheduling link, the full public booking URL, with protocol.
# This is the ONLY thing /book cannot work without, and it is not
# something that can be guessed: the wrong link books a stranger's
# calendar.
#
#   Calendly     https://calendly.com/<handle>/<event>
#   Cal.com      https://cal.com/<handle>/<event>
#   Zoho / GHL / Google Appointments: whatever the team already uses
#
# A calendly.com link is embedded with Calendly's own inline widget,
# which sizes itself and accepts prefill. Anything else is embedded as a
# plain iframe. Both work; nothing needs changing in the code either
# way. If the scheduler refuses to be framed (some GHL and Google
# setups send X-Frame-Options), the page falls back to an "open the
# booking page in a new tab" link after twelve seconds.
#
# Read by: src/components/book/BookingPage.tsx.
#
# WITHOUT IT: /book renders a clearly labelled stand-in at the exact
# height the calendar will occupy, telling whoever sees it to email
# support. The rest of the page (the payment confirmation, the GA4
# purchase, the footer) works normally. It is loud on purpose: a paying
# buyer must never meet an empty box.


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# RAZORPAY  ·  Dashboard -> Account & Settings
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# API Keys page. The key id starts rzp_test_ or rzp_live_ and is 23
# characters; the secret is 24 and is shown ONCE at generation.
#
# The test/live mode of the deployment is DERIVED from the prefix of the
# key id (see isTestMode in src/lib/checkout-config.ts), so there is no
# separate IS_TEST flag to forget to flip.
#
# WITHOUT THEM: /api/razorpay/create-order returns 503 and the checkout
# tells the buyer "Payments are not switched on yet."
RAZORPAY_KEY_ID=
RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET=

# ⚠️ A SEPARATE VALUE FROM THE API KEYS. It is on the Webhooks page
# (Account & Settings -> Webhooks), not the API Keys page, and you
# choose it yourself when you register the webhook.
#
# Register: <NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL>/api/razorpay/webhook
# Active event: payment.captured  (that one, and no others)
#
# WITHOUT IT: the webhook returns 500 to Razorpay on every call, so
# Meta's Purchase and GA4's server-side purchase NEVER FIRE. The site
# still takes money and the buyer still reaches the booking page, so
# nothing looks broken from the outside. This is the single most
# expensive blank line in the file.
RAZORPAY_WEBHOOK_SECRET=


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# META  ·  Events Manager -> Data Sources -> your dataset
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# The same pixel id, twice. NEXT_PUBLIC_ is inlined into the browser
# bundle for the base pixel code; the unprefixed one is read server-side
# by the CAPI routes. Two names because Next only exposes NEXT_PUBLIC_
# vars to the client, and shipping the server one to the browser would
# be a habit worth not forming.
NEXT_PUBLIC_META_PIXEL_ID=
META_PIXEL_ID=

# Conversions API access token: dataset -> Settings -> Conversions API
# -> Generate access token. A long EAA... string.
#
# WITHOUT IT: capiReady() is false, every server-side Meta event is
# skipped silently, and Events Manager shows only browser PageViews.
META_CAPI_ACCESS_TOKEN=

# ⚠️ REMOVE THIS BEFORE LAUNCH. Events sent with a test event code go to
# the Test Events tab and DO NOT COUNT toward optimisation, so a live
# campaign with this set is buying blind. Take it from Events Manager ->
# Test Events while testing, then delete the value.
#
# It also flips isTestMode(), which is what keeps a staging purchase
# distinguishable from a real one.
META_CAPI_TEST_EVENT_CODE=


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# GA4  ·  Admin -> Data Streams -> your web stream
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Measurement ID, the G-XXXXXXXXXX at the top of the stream.
#
# WITHOUT IT: <Analytics /> renders no base tag, so window.gtag never
# exists, so view_item / add_to_cart / begin_checkout / add_payment_info
# and the browser copy of purchase are all silent no-ops. The site looks
# completely healthy while GA4 records nothing above the revenue line.
NEXT_PUBLIC_GA4_ID=

# Measurement Protocol API secret: same stream -> Measurement Protocol
# API secrets -> Create. A short opaque string, NOT the measurement id.
#
# WITHOUT IT: the Razorpay webhook cannot send GA4 its server-side
# purchase, so GA4 counts only buyers who come back to the tab. In India
# a UPI payer often does not, so GA4 revenue reads low against Razorpay.
GA4_API_SECRET=


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# PABBLY  ·  Connect -> your workflow -> the Webhook trigger step
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# The trigger's "Webhook URL", copied from the first step of the
# workflow. Looks like
# https://connect.pabbly.com/workflow/sendwebhookdata/...
#
# This is FULFILMENT, not analytics. It is the hand-off that tells the
# automation WHO bought, so the buyer gets their booking link, their
# reminders and a row Sandesh can read before he takes the call. It is
# also the ONLY place a full unhashed record of a sale exists anywhere:
# Meta receives SHA-256 hashes, GA4 receives no PII at all, and Razorpay
# holds only what it needs to charge a card. That is why the payload
# carries the Meta match keys as well as the buyer's details.
#
# WITHOUT IT: the sale is still tracked in Meta and GA4, and the buyer
# still receives nothing. That failure is invisible in every dashboard
# you would think to check.
#
# ⚠️ Build the workflow and push ONE test payment through it BEFORE the
# first real sale. Pabbly builds its field map from the FIRST payload
# the trigger ever receives, so a workflow whose first payload is
# half-populated cannot map the missing columns later without re-running
# the trigger. Every key is emitted on every call for exactly this
# reason, empty string where unknown. Never remove a key once a step
# maps it: removing one does not error, it silently blanks a column.
PABBLY_WEBHOOK_URL=


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# CLARITY  ·  clarity.microsoft.com -> project -> Setup
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# The project id from the install snippet. Session recordings and
# heatmaps only; it is not part of the conversion rail.
#
# WITHOUT IT: no Clarity tag renders. Nothing else is affected.
NEXT_PUBLIC_CLARITY_ID=


# =====================================================================
# REQUIRED BEFORE LAUNCH, BUT NOT ENV
# =====================================================================
# 1. Register the Razorpay webhook (URL and event above), and put its
#    secret in RAZORPAY_WEBHOOK_SECRET.
# 2. Delete META_CAPI_TEST_EVENT_CODE.
# 3. Replace the https://example.com literal in BOTH
#    src/app/layout.tsx (FALLBACK_ORIGIN) and
#    src/lib/checkout-config.ts (fallbackEventSourceUrl).
# 4. src/app/_legal/legal.ts: `effectiveDate` must match the day the
#    policies actually go live, and `entity` must match the PAN record
#    character for character.
# 5. Build the Pabbly workflow, push one test payment through it, and map
#    every column in a single sitting. A column mapped later is a re-run
#    of the trigger.
# 7. Everything else still open is listed in PENDING.md: the assets, the
#    guarantee-versus-booking-fee microcopy, the mechanism beat.
